pcm: make calc_tv's envelope index a template parameter

`e` is a literal at all four call sites (1, 0, 1, 2) and selects which envelope
is being stepped, but it is passed as a runtime argument, so gcc emits one
out-of-line .constprop clone that all the e == 2 calls share -- 2.97M calls in a
0.4s benchmark, each paying a call, a prologue and an epilogue for a body whose
volmul half is dead. e == 2 passes volmul == NULL and needs none of that
arithmetic, and its `e != 2 || active` tests collapse to `active`.

Making `e` a template parameter lets each instantiation drop its dead half. Two
uses of the intermediates `w1` and `w2`, which patch 0001 removed in favour of
the packed type table, are re-derived in place: w2 is type bit 0 and w1 is
(speed & 0xf0) == 0.

Measured on the ROM-free voice-loop harness, all 32 voices keyed on:
31543 -> 29751 Ir per tick (-5.7%). Static size of PCM_Update on aarch64 grows
7700 -> 8060 bytes, which is nothing against a 32 KiB I-cache.

--- a/src/backend/pcm.cpp
+++ b/src/backend/pcm.cpp
@@ -381,7 +381,13 @@
     t.write[4]  = 1;
 }
 
-inline void calc_tv(pcm_t& pcm, const tv_taps& taps, int e, int adjust, uint16_t *levelcur, int active, int *volmul)
+// `e` selects which of the three envelopes is being stepped and is a literal at
+// every call site.  Making it a template parameter lets the compiler drop the
+// dead half of the function per instantiation - in particular the e == 2 case,
+// which is called once per voice slot with volmul == NULL and therefore needs
+// none of the volmul arithmetic at all.
+template <int e>
+inline void calc_tv(pcm_t& pcm, const tv_taps& taps, int adjust, uint16_t *levelcur, int active, int *volmul)
 {
     // int adjust = ram2[3+e];
     // int levelcur = ram2[9+e] & 0x7fff;
